# Spec & Contract Rules

## Spec-First Workflow

1. Create FEATURES.md entry BEFORE coding
2. Write acceptance criteria in `.agentic/spec/contracts/F-XXXX.yaml`
3. Write failing tests from ACs
4. Implement to make tests pass
5. Update specs to reflect what was built

## Contract Format

```yaml
id: F-XXXX
name: Feature Name
lifecycle: planned|implementing|shipped
assertions:
  - id: AC-001
    text: "Testable behavior description"
    type: structural|behavioral
    verify: "shell command that returns 0 on pass"
```

## Commands

- `ag spec F-XXXX` — create/update spec
- `ag contract check F-XXXX` — verify assertions pass
- `ag contract coverage` — see test coverage across contracts
- `ag contract pending` — find contracts needing user input
- `ag migrate-specs` — convert markdown ACs to YAML contracts

## Rules

- Shipped contracts are protected — use migrations to add new ACs
- NFR constraints belong in testable ACs, not separate sections
- Run `ag intel spec [F-XXXX]` before writing specs for quality guidance
